I’ll implement the contract as a three-state scanner: skip leading Python whitespace after each delimiter, recognize an initial `I`, and count only when its next character is a literal space (matching the task’s “word `I`” boundary). This avoids unsupported regex/split operations and gives the proof a clean structural invariant over the remaining character sequence.
