The end-to-end claim’s recursive target itself triggers backend narrowing before the already-proved loop lemma can be applied. I’m expressing the same proof compositionally: one acyclic claim proves that an arbitrary function call reaches the state-0 loop invariant, and the three mutual invariant claims prove that state reaches the specified result. This avoids asking the backend to eagerly evaluate an infinite symbolic target while preserving the full call-to-result argument.
